{
 "name": "VAOPGCPREC 19-90, Jun 15, 1990, Applicability of Public Law No. 101-237, Section 111 - 306 Pension",
 "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center\">\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">Decision Assessment Document<br />\tVAOPGCPREC 19-90, Jun 15, 1990, Applicability of Public Law No. 101-237, Section 111 - 306 Pension<br />\tOffice of General Counsel Precedent Opinion</span></span></p><p>\t&nbsp;</p><p>\t<strong><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">What the opinion is about:</span></span></strong></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">Applicability of Public Law No. 101-237, Section 111 - 306 Pension.</span></span></p><p>\t<strong><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">Impact on VBA:</span></span></strong></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">None.</span></span></p><p>\t<strong><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">Summary of the facts and findings:</span></span></strong></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">See OGC opinion for facts.</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">The provisions of section 111 of Pub.L. No. 101-237, which amend 38 U.S.C. \u00a7 3203 (a) to liberalize the laws governing reduction of pension payable to institutionalized veterans without dependents, do not apply to veterans receiving section-306 pension, i.e., pension payable under laws in effect on December 31, 1978, which arose out of the 1960 revisions to the pension laws pursuant to Pub.L. No. 86-211, or to veterans receiving old-law pension, i.e., pension payable under laws in effect on June 30, 1960, and protected after enactment of Pub.L. No. 86-211.</span></span></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">The increase in the amount payable to institutionalized pensioners without dependents provided for in section 307 of Pub.L. No. 95-588 should not have been applied to veterans receiving section-306 pension.</span></span></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">References:</span></span></strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><a href=\"http://www.va.gov/ogc/docs/1990/PREC_19-90.doc\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px\">http://www.va.gov/ogc/docs/1990/PREC_19-90.doc</span></span></a></span></span></p><p>\t&nbsp;</p>",
